# Module
Module194281Name = Variable BOM
Module194281Desc = One BOM for all the variants of a product, resolved for each variant to produce
VariableBom = Variable BOM
VariableBomSetup = Variable BOM setup
VariableBomSetupDesc = A variable BOM is a BOM of a parent product with variants, ticked "Variable BOM" on its card. Its lines flagged "Matched to variant" use a parent product with variants, and the variant consumed is resolved from the variant to produce.
VariableBomTab = Variants
VariableBomHelp = This BOM is a variable BOM: one manufacturing order can be created for each variant of its product, and the lines marked "Matched to variant" are replaced by the matching variant of their component. Open the Variants tab to set the rules and check every variant.
VariableBomHowTo = How to use
VariableBomHowTo1 = Create a BOM for the parent product that has variants (for example "Shirt", not "Shirt L Red") and tick "Variable BOM" on it.
VariableBomHowTo2 = Add the lines. For a component that exists in variants (a blank tee in every size and color), add its parent product and tick "Matched to variant": the manufacturing order will consume the variant with the same attribute values as the shirt produced.
VariableBomHowTo3 = Open the Variants tab of the BOM. Set a fixed value for an attribute the produced product does not have (for example the weight of a thread), and quantities that depend on an attribute (more ink for size L). The tab shows for how many variants each line can be resolved.
VariableBomHowTo4 = Validate the BOM and click "Create MO". Choose the variant to produce with the attribute selects; the components that will be consumed are listed below them.
VariableBomHowTo5 = The hook of the core (see below) must be available, otherwise manufacturing orders of variable BOMs are refused.
VariableBomTabIntro = This BOM produces a product with variants. Each manufacturing order produces one variant; this tab defines how the lines are adapted to it:
VariableBomTabStep1 = A line "Matched to variant" (ticked on the BOM card) consumes the variant of its component with the same attribute values as the variant produced.
VariableBomTabStep2 = For an attribute of the component that the produced product does not have, set a fixed value in the rules of the line (pencil at the end of the row).
VariableBomTabStep3 = The quantity of any line can depend on one attribute of the variant produced (0 = the line is not used for that value).
VariableBomTabStep4 = "Resolution" tells for how many variants the line can be resolved, and the folder icon unfolds the result for each one. All lines must reach all variants before creating manufacturing orders.
VariableBomRulesHelp = Fixed attribute values and quantities by variant defined for the line. Click the pencil at the end of the row to edit them in place.
VariableBomResolutionHelp = Variants to produce for which this line can be resolved, out of all of them. Orange means some cannot: unfold the line (folder icon) to see which, then edit its rules; an attribute may need a fixed value, or the component may not exist in that variant.
VariableBomQtyByVariantHelp = Choose the attribute of the produced product that changes the quantity, then enter a quantity for each of its values. Empty = the quantity of the line, 0 = the line is not used for that value.
VariableBomPreviewHelp = Show what this line becomes for each variant of the product to produce. Check it before validating the BOM.
VariableBomLineNotMatchedNote = This line is not matched to variant: the same product is consumed for every variant, only its quantity can change. To consume a variant of it instead, edit the line on the BOM card and tick "Matched to variant".
VariableBomVariantToProduceHelp = Choose one value for each attribute. The product to produce is set automatically, and the components that will be consumed are listed below.
VariableBomSuffix = (Variable BOM)

# Core hook
VariableBomCoreHook = Hook processBOMLines of Dolibarr core
VariableBomCoreHookOk = Available
VariableBomCoreHookDesc = Needed to resolve the lines of a manufacturing order. Proposed to Dolibarr; until it is merged, apply the patch provided with the module (core-patch directory).
ErrorVariableBomCoreHookMissing = Your Dolibarr version does not have the hook processBOMLines needed by the Variable BOM module: manufacturing orders of variable BOMs are refused. Apply the core patch provided with the module.

# BOM
VariableBomFlag = Variable BOM
VariableBomFlagHelp = Tick to make this BOM a variable BOM: one BOM for every variant of its product. The product to produce must be the parent product with variants. The rules of the lines are then set in the Variants tab.
VariableBomNbVariants = %s variants to produce, see the Variants tab
VariableBomNotVariable = This BOM is not a variable BOM. To use this tab, tick "Variable BOM" on the BOM card; its product to produce must have variants.
VariableBomLineMatch = Matched to variant
VariableBomLineMatchHelp = Tick when the product of the line exists in variants (e.g. a blank tee in every size and color): the manufacturing order consumes the variant with the same attribute values as the variant produced. The product of the line must be the parent product, not one of its variants. Rules per attribute are set in the Variants tab.
VariableBomLines = Lines of the BOM (for %s variants to produce)
VariableBomReadOnlyValidated = This BOM is validated, so its variant rules are read-only (like its lines). To change them, open the %s and click "Back to draft", edit the rules here, then validate the BOM again.
VariableBomReadOnlyNoPermission = Your account can not modify BOMs, so the variant rules are shown read-only.
VariableBomRules = Variant rules
VariableBomRulesOfLine = Variant rules of line
VariableBomRulesSaved = Variant rules saved
VariableBomResolution = Resolution
VariableBomResolvedCount = Resolved for %s of %s variants
VariableBomComponentAttributes = Attributes of the component
VariableBomComponentAttributesHelp = For each attribute of the component, choose whether its value follows the variant to produce or is always the same value.
VariableBomSameAsProduced = Same as variant to produce
VariableBomChooseValue = Choose a value (attribute not on the product to produce)
VariableBomQtyByVariant = Quantity by variant
VariableBomQtyAttribute = Quantity varies by
VariableBomQtyNone = Same quantity for all variants
VariableBomQtyHelp = Leave empty to use the quantity of the line (%s). Use 0 if the line is not used for this value.
VariableBomQtySummary = Qty by %s: %s
VariableBomPreview = Result for each variant to produce
VariableBomShowAllResults = Show the results of every line
VariableBomHideAllResults = Hide the results
VariableBomNotUsed = Not used

# MO
VariableBomVariantToProduce = Variant to produce
VariableBomSelectVariant = Select the variant to produce to see the components that will be consumed.

# Errors
ErrorVariableBomFlagNeedsVariants = "Variable BOM" can be ticked only when the product to produce has variants.
ErrorVariableBomMatchNeedsVariableBom = A line can be matched to variant only on a variable BOM: tick "Variable BOM" on the BOM card first (its product must have variants).
ErrorVariableBomMatchNeedsVariantParent = A line can be matched to variant only if its product is a parent product with variants.
ErrorVariableBomVariantToProduceRequired = This BOM is a variable BOM: the product to produce must be a variant of %s.
ErrorVariableBomAttributeNotDefined = Component %s: no value for attribute(s) %s. Set a fixed value in the variant rules of the line.
ErrorVariableBomNoVariantFound = Component %s: no variant exists for %s.
ErrorVariableBomNoVariantForValues = No variant of %s exists for the selected values.

# Debug
DebugMode = Debug Mode
DebugModeDesc = When enabled, exposes a diagnostic endpoint at /custom/variablebom/ajax/debug.php for troubleshooting (module status, core hook, resolution of a BOM).
